        // ── THE CHALLENGE ─────────────────────────────────────────────
        section#cns-challenge.cns-challenge.page-section
            .container.px-4.px-lg-5
                .row.justify-content-center.mb-5
                    .col-lg-8.text-center
                        span.cns-section-eyebrow The Challenge
                        h2.cns-section-heading.mt-3 Why Most AI Investments Fall Short
                .row.gx-5.align-items-center
                    .col-lg-6
                        .cns-challenge-lead
                            p Most enterprises struggle to realize ROI from AI, even as individuals see dramatic productivity gains.
                        .cns-challenge-body.mt-4
                            p Off-the-shelf tools and ad-hoc prompting aren&rsquo;t enough to enhance company-specific workflows or competitive advantages. In-house experiments often spiral into cost overruns, wasted effort, and misalignment with business goals.
                            p.mt-3 The truth is, most breakthrough AI systems are finely tuned for a specific task. If your company&rsquo;s solutions aren&rsquo;t another copy in the crowd, why should your AI be? When it isn&rsquo;t tailored to the problems you actually face, results are bound to be underwhelming.
                    .col-lg-6.mt-4.mt-lg-0
                        .cns-insight-card
                            .cns-insight-label
                                i.fas.fa-lightbulb
                                | &ensp;The Core Insight
                            blockquote.cns-insight-quote
                                | &ldquo;Real success demands domain expertise, rigorous design, and deep workflow integration.&rdquo;
                            p.cns-insight-foot
                                | AI delivers only when it&rsquo;s built for your business&mdash;not simply bought or borrowed.


